From 135a4becefa1bdf8c204790e1ce4df200d412dc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tawheed Makhdoomi <_@tawheed.cc>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:54:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/41] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8180x-microsoft-surface-pro-x:
 Describe the cameras

Describe the three camera sensors of the Surface Pro X. From the Windows
DSDT (PEP power sequences of \_SB.CAMS/CAMF/CAMI and their SCFG methods):

  rear  OV13858 @0x10: MCLK0 19.2 MHz, reset GPIO22, L14A 1.8 V, L17A 2.85 V,
                       L1A 1.2 V
  front OV5693  @0x36: MCLK2 19.2 MHz, reset GPIO12, L14A 1.8 V
  IR    OV7251  @0x60: MCLK3 19.2 MHz, enable GPIO23, L14A 1.8 V

L1A, L14A and L17A are voted only by the camera devices in the DSDT.

The ACPI tables do not say which CCI master or CSIPHY each sensor uses. The
nodes follow the Qualcomm SM8150 MTP reference slots for MCLK0/2/3 (rear on
CCI0 master 0 + CSIPHY0, front on CCI0 master 1 + CSIPHY2, IR on CCI1 master
1 + CSIPHY3). This is a guess, to be checked on hardware.

The rear module's DW9800 VCM and the M24C64 EEPROMs are not described yet.

Signed-off-by: Tawheed Makhdoomi <_@tawheed.cc>
